"""Streaming arrival comparison slide."""

from surface import Frame, NodeKind, Slide, attr, group, heading, line_break, node, paragraph, prose, span, text

pub def slide_streaming_arrival_comparison() -> Slide:
    return Slide(
        slug="streaming-arrival-comparison",
        title="Micro-batch and Real-time processing",
        frame=Frame.Composed,
        styles="slide streaming-slide ss-arrival-compare-slide",
        content=[
            group([
            text("07 / STRUCTURED STREAMING"),
        ], style="eyebrow"),
            heading("Micro-batch and Real-time processing", level=1),
            prose("Follow record C, arriving after processing has started.", style="ss-arrival-lead"),
            node(NodeKind.Figure, children=[
            node(NodeKind.Svg, children=[
                node(NodeKind.SvgTitle, content="When a new record can enter the running query", attributes=[attr("id", "ss-ac-title")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgDescription, content="Record C arrives at the same point in both timelines: micro-batch holds it for Batch 2 because Batch 1 has fixed input, while Real-time tasks can process C during their ongoing run.", attributes=[attr("id", "ss-ac-desc")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgDefinitions, children=[
                    node(NodeKind.SvgMarker, children=[
                        node(NodeKind.SvgPath, attributes=[attr("d", "M0 0L8 3L0 6Z"), attr("fill", "#67747b")]),
                    ], attributes=[attr("id", "ss-ac-arrow"), attr("markerWidth", "8"), attr("markerHeight", "6"), attr("refX", "7"), attr("refY", "3"), attr("orient", "auto")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgMarker, children=[
                        node(NodeKind.SvgPath, attributes=[attr("d", "M0 0L8 3L0 6Z"), attr("fill", "#a66714")]),
                    ], attributes=[attr("id", "ss-ac-arrow-wait"), attr("markerWidth", "8"), attr("markerHeight", "6"), attr("refX", "7"), attr("refY", "3"), attr("orient", "auto")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgMarker, children=[
                        node(NodeKind.SvgPath, attributes=[attr("d", "M0 0L8 3L0 6Z"), attr("fill", "#4b7c35")]),
                    ], attributes=[attr("id", "ss-ac-arrow-run"), attr("markerWidth", "8"), attr("markerHeight", "6"), attr("refX", "7"), attr("refY", "3"), attr("orient", "auto")]),
                ]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Earlier", style="ss-ac-small", attributes=[attr("x", "280"), attr("y", "22")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Same arrivals · no latency scale", style="ss-ac-caption", attributes=[attr("x", "824"), attr("y", "22"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Later →", style="ss-ac-small", attributes=[attr("x", "1284"), attr("y", "22"), attr("text-anchor", "end")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgLine, style="ss-ac-rule", attributes=[attr("x1", "280"), attr("y1", "36"), attr("x2", "1284"), attr("y2", "36")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgLine, style="ss-ac-rule", attributes=[attr("x1", "616"), attr("y1", "30"), attr("x2", "616"), attr("y2", "42")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ss-ac-wait-arrow", attributes=[attr("d", "M672 86H956Q964 86 964 94V142")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ss-ac-arrow", attributes=[attr("d", "M876 184H946")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ss-ac-run-arrow", attributes=[attr("d", "M616 296V330")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Micro-batch", style="ss-ac-mode", attributes=[attr("x", "0"), attr("y", "178")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="New tasks per batch", style="ss-ac-small", attributes=[attr("x", "0"), attr("y", "210")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-record", attributes=[attr("x", "560"), attr("y", "64"), attr("width", "112"), attr("height", "44"), attr("rx", "4")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Record C", style="ss-ac-record-text", attributes=[attr("x", "616"), attr("y", "93"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, attributes=[attr("x", "748"), attr("y", "51"), attr("width", "244"), attr("height", "28"), attr("fill", "#fafaf8")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Waits for Batch 2", style="ss-ac-wait-label", attributes=[attr("x", "870"), attr("y", "72"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-batch", attributes=[attr("x", "280"), attr("y", "144"), attr("width", "596"), attr("height", "80"), attr("rx", "6")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Batch 1", style="ss-ac-batch-title", attributes=[attr("x", "578"), attr("y", "178"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Processes A and B", style="ss-ac-detail", attributes=[attr("x", "578"), attr("y", "208"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-batch", attributes=[attr("x", "948"), attr("y", "144"), attr("width", "336"), attr("height", "80"), attr("rx", "6")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Batch 2", style="ss-ac-batch-title", attributes=[attr("x", "1116"), attr("y", "178"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Processes C", style="ss-ac-detail", attributes=[attr("x", "1116"), attr("y", "208"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Real-time", style="ss-ac-mode", attributes=[attr("x", "0"), attr("y", "358")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Tasks keep running", style="ss-ac-small", attributes=[attr("x", "0"), attr("y", "390")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-record", attributes=[attr("x", "560"), attr("y", "252"), attr("width", "112"), attr("height", "44"), attr("rx", "4")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Record C", style="ss-ac-record-text", attributes=[attr("x", "616"), attr("y", "281"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Enters the running tasks", style="ss-ac-run-label", attributes=[attr("x", "704"), attr("y", "281")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-running", attributes=[attr("x", "280"), attr("y", "332"), attr("width", "1004"), attr("height", "64"), attr("rx", "6")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="A, B…", style="ss-ac-detail", attributes=[attr("x", "360"), attr("y", "372")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, style="ss-ac-processing", attributes=[attr("x", "616"), attr("y", "344"), attr("width", "176"), attr("height", "40"), attr("rx", "4")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Process C", style="ss-ac-process-text", attributes=[attr("x", "704"), attr("y", "372"), attr("text-anchor", "middle")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="…keep accepting records", style="ss-ac-detail", attributes=[attr("x", "816"), attr("y", "372")]),
            ], attributes=[attr("viewBox", "0 0 1308 416"), attr("role", "img"), attr("aria-labelledby", "ss-ac-title ss-ac-desc")]),
        ], style="ss-arrival-compare"),
            paragraph([
            text("A micro-batch fixes its input before it runs."),
            line_break(),
            span("Real-time tasks keep accepting new records during the run."),
        ], style="ss-takeaway"),
            node(NodeKind.Footer, children=[
            span("Danny’s Code Corner"),
            span("86"),
        ]),
        ],
        notes="""Use the same compatible stateless Kafka query from the preceding Real-time slide. A, B and C label records, not partitions or tasks. Both lanes show the same arrival history. The horizontal positions explain ordering, not benchmark timings.

Start at Batch 1. Spark has chosen a bounded slice containing A and B. C reaches Kafka after that input boundary was fixed, while Batch 1 is still running. C cannot join Batch 1; it waits at the source until a later batch includes it. In this small example that is Batch 2. Admission limits or a backlog can defer it further. The default trigger already starts the next batch as soon as the previous batch finishes; the wait drawn here is not an optional five-second timer.

Now follow the same C on the lower lane. The Real-time tasks are already running and can read the newly available record through the same stateless pipeline. They do not need a new micro-batch and a fresh task set to admit C. Processing, source polling and sink delivery still take time; spare capacity is assumed. Real-time also checkpoints progress periodically, as explained on 72. It does not eliminate every boundary or guarantee zero latency.

The distinction is input admission and task lifetime. Do not say micro-batch writes always wait until the batch ends: some sinks emit while tasks process the bounded slice. This figure also does not claim the original word-count query is supported in every Real-time runtime. Operator and connector support remains version-dependent.

Transition: we have compared how the work runs. Return to the micro-batch word count to explain which result rows the output mode sends to the sink.

Sources checked 20 September 2026: https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/streaming/apis-on-dataframes-and-datasets.html#triggers ; https://apache.github.io/spark/streaming/real-time-mode.html#how-real-time-mode-works (in-progress architecture documentation, not a pinned 4.2 support matrix) ; https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/structured-streaming/real-time/concepts""",
    )
